{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423633","formula":"F₂O₂S","hill":"F2O2S","elements":["O","F","S"],"composition":{"F":2.0,"O":2.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sulfuryl fluoride","ru":"Сульфурилфторид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sulfuryl fluoride (also spelled sulphuryl fluoride) is an inorganic compound with the formula SO2F2. It is an easily condensed gas and has properties more similar to sulfur hexafluoride than sulfuryl chloride, being resistant to hydrolysis even up to 150 °C. It is neurotoxic and a potent greenhouse gas, but is widely used as a fumigant insecticide to control termites.","ru":"Сульфурѝлфтори́д — неорганическое соединение серы(VI), кислорода и фтора с формулой SO2F2 (может рассматриваться как оксофторид серы). Бесцветный газ (при нормальных условиях) без запаха. Молекула сульфурилфторида имеет конфигурацию искажённого тетраэдра, с расположенным в центре шестивалентным атомом серы."},"fame":23,"pubchemCid":17607,"mass":102.06,"charge":0,"smiles":"O=S(=O)(F)F","inchikey":"OBTWBSRJZRCYQV-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"sulfuryl difluoride","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"17607","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":-0.106,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.004,"y":-1.268,"z":0.844,"el":"F"},{"x":0.005,"y":1.268,"z":0.844,"el":"F"},{"x":1.274,"y":-0.005,"z":-0.791,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.274,"y":0.004,"z":-0.791,"el":"O"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[0,3,2],[0,4,2]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q423633","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulfuryl_fluoride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D1%83%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%84%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%84%D1%82%D0%BE